Subject: [PATCH 1/2] emacs: Fold org-style headings in notmuch-show
To: Pat Maddox <pat@patmaddox.com>
Cc: lab-devel@p7x.dev
Change-Id: yukztumuzvvtmypovmyskqmlpxxvmqnm
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 03:17:30 +0000

Long agent replies are hard to navigate in notmuch-show, which can
only collapse whole messages. Letting each "* " heading in a
text/plain part fold its section gives the expand and collapse of
org-mode without leaving the mail.

Mail on the list is untrusted, so the headings are found with a
regexp and folded with overlays. Org-mode never runs on a message.
Turning on org-mode has run Lisp and shell commands from the text it
was turned on for, as the Emacs 29.3 and 29.4 security releases
record. Each heading is a notmuch-style button, so TAB reaches it
and RET toggles it, and its face is the outline face for its level.
A section ends at the next heading of its level or above, or at the
end of its part, so folding never hides the next message.
